                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1d0d7a7-59c7-3ad9-b145-c3425df0a758",
                                        "entry_id": "4482d0e4-743a-322a-b760-651bf1c449b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unspecified large number (of)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "excessive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a8816c2-dcd4-4f0f-81a8-d1b50b107097",
                                                "sense_id": "f1d0d7a7-59c7-3ad9-b145-c3425df0a758",
                                                "text": "Even if you are not a transistor collector, it is still pretty neat seeing that many early transistors. Wowzers...yes indeed...wowzers! Ok...it is not a gazillion but sure is a bunch."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a021fc6e-4c36-49f0-8d97-729e4fef1db1",
                                                "sense_id": "f1d0d7a7-59c7-3ad9-b145-c3425df0a758",
                                                "text": "First, he is merely following laws written by nativist Republicans. This is a cop-out. As president he sets priorities for the executive branch, which cannot catch and prosecute everyone who breaks any of the gazillions of federal rules."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "65bc21d0-5f7c-40b3-802e-60cc9c106862",
                        "source_entry_id": "746e45a7-d49c-300f-88d2-44f903099d2d",
                        "source_sense_id": "fc133a25-2bf6-3a01-b9ad-a2fa23ee770e",
                        "target_lang_word": "gagillion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gagillion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "16040f65-36f1-31a2-a29b-04d6c3b78642",
                                        "entry_id": "de82549e-6dc6-363d-a47d-500a8b85a9a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unspecified large number (of)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "excessive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cf4e370-ec53-4cf4-ace7-f752326d714c",
                                                "sense_id": "16040f65-36f1-31a2-a29b-04d6c3b78642",
                                                "text": "The brochures basically told the same story Stan had given me: Pacific Properties owned a gagillion places that generated a gagillion dollars. The implication was that if you didn't invest you just didn't care about making easy money with no risk whatsoever to your original investment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ca46ca2-5ab5-49d5-827a-922ea8f4390a",
                                                "sense_id": "16040f65-36f1-31a2-a29b-04d6c3b78642",
                                                "text": "Plus, there are about a thousand things that also could, or should get done in that time: a load of laundry, loading the dishwasher, tidying the kitchen, picking up a gagillion toys and blankies off the ground, restocking the change tables."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "530079c0-8159-406d-8563-e77deaceaaea",
                        "source_entry_id": "746e45a7-d49c-300f-88d2-44f903099d2d",
                        "source_sense_id": "fc133a25-2bf6-3a01-b9ad-a2fa23ee770e",
                        "target_lang_word": "gajillion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gajillion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8696090f-dd07-3ae0-96c0-c202119b5e25",
                                        "entry_id": "7a3fbd49-1b56-316d-b231-9738fd83e9b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unspecified large number (of); a gazillion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "excessive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7916be17-fcfc-4fe7-b774-a6bb65f6161d",
                                                "sense_id": "8696090f-dd07-3ae0-96c0-c202119b5e25",
                                                "text": "When Anna gets home from school, Cody is sitting on the step in front of the purple door, juggling his knees. \"Ben and Cass walked by a gajillion minutes ago. What took you so long?\"\n A gajillion minutes? Really?\" Anna had let the others get ahead, but she never lost sight of them.\n \"Okay, maybe only half a gajillion,\" he admits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bd738b8-61e1-4243-a2eb-dd3185a28da2",
                                                "sense_id": "8696090f-dd07-3ae0-96c0-c202119b5e25",
                                                "text": "We humans and other complex animals are full of microbes, gajillions of them. People have so many that microbe cells living in our bodies outnumber our own vastly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "791d0644-9c2e-4ca3-9de6-f1af8d91bb88",
                                                "sense_id": "8696090f-dd07-3ae0-96c0-c202119b5e25",
                                                "text": "Starbucks wants to sell a gajillion lattes and Frappuccinos. But it also wants to make the world a better place. What's wrong with that exactly?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb3d2611-53c9-4a4f-9659-b0c543a5e5da",
                                                "sense_id": "8696090f-dd07-3ae0-96c0-c202119b5e25",
                                                "text": "\"You like Miss Winnie, don't you, Uncle Ben? Because I like Miss Winnie a gajillion times.\" Ben's chuckle floated to her ears. \"I like Miss Winnie a gajillion times, too.\" Winnie hid her face in her shoulder as the hot sun beat down on her and she was overwhelmed with emotion. A gajillion was a lot of like. But she was sure she liked Ben and Lola a gajillion times more."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
